[center][size=6][b]YADS - Yet Another Digital Storage Mod[/b][/size]
[size=3][i]Network storage for Fields of Mistria. One search bar for every crate you own.[/i][/size]

[b]Beta 1.2[/b] by mykay · requires the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fieldsofmistria/mods/78]Mods of Mistria Installer[/url] 0.15.1+[/center]

[line]

[b]Back up your saves before installing any mod. It's a beta.[/b]

If you've played modded Minecraft or Terraria you already know the idea. This is my love letter to Applied Energistics 2, Refined Storage and Magic Storage: link storage units into a network and browse all of it from one terminal. Search, sort, filter, quick-stack.

[size=5][b]The units[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Storage Heart[/b] (50 Wood, 5 Copper Ingot, 1 Glass). The brain. One per network.
[*][b]Storage Block[/b] (30 Wood, 1 Copper Ingot). 30 slots each. Chain as many as you want.
[*][b]Access Panel[/b] (1 Copper Ingot, 1 Glass). The terminal. Open it to browse the network.
[*][b]Remote Access Panel[/b] (5 Ruby, 5 Sapphire, 5 Copper Ingot, 5 Iron Ingot, 1 Access Panel). Browse from anywhere.
[/list]

Crafted at the Woodcrafting Station, under "Chests & Storage" and their own "Digital Storage" category.

Place units so they touch and they link up. Connected units glow (blocks tint green, yellow or red by how full they are), a disconnected one shows a sad face. Each room is its own network, so the farm and the farmhouse each need their own Heart. Don't place units on tables.

[size=5][b]Remote access[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Hand the Remote Access Panel to a Storage Heart and they're linked. Press [b]F6[/b] anywhere to browse that network, even from the bottom of the mines.
[*]Several networks? [b]Hold[/b] the key for a picker: one row per network with room, blocks and fill. Tick the checkbox on a row to make it your default, and a tap goes straight there.
[*][b]Rebind the key in game[/b]: hold the key, click Rebind key, press the one you want. Works instantly. Holding F6 always opens the picker as a backup, so a bad key can never lock you out.
[*]To unlink, take the remote back out at an Access Panel. You can't pull it out through a remote view, so you can't strand yourself from the mines.
[/list]

[size=5][b]The network view[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]The vanilla storage UI over every connected unit at once. Withdraw and deposit exactly like a chest.
[*]A real search box: full text editing, an X to clear it, Ctrl+arrows jump whole words. Auto-focus toggle so it's ready when the panel opens.
[*]14 category filters, plus a "Museum needs" lens for what the museum still wants.
[*]Value badges per stack or per item. Big numbers abbreviate, like 12.3k.
[*]Five sort modes. Your pick is remembered.
[*]Quick-stack your backpack into the network with one button.
[*]Crafting stations pull from the network automatically. The units are real chests, so it just works.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Good to know[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]You can squeeze between crates: solid core, walkable edges.
[*]A unit that still holds items takes five pickaxe swings to break. Empty ones break in one.
[*]Blocks with no heart behave as plain chests, so your items are never locked away.
[*]If a deposit doesn't fit, the rest comes straight back with a toast. Nothing is silently eaten.
[/list]

The mod never holds your items. Everything lives in the real chest inventories of the placed units, which the game's own save system writes. If the game crashes with the view open, nothing is lost.

[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Extract the zip into [font=Courier New]Fields of Mistria/mods/[/font] so the file [font=Courier New]mods/yads/manifest.json[/font] exists.
[*]Run the Mods of Mistria Installer, tick [b]YADS[/b], hit Install.
[*]Play. Recipes unlock automatically, existing saves included.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Before uninstalling[/b][/size]

[b]Empty your units first.[/b] The engine drops placed objects it no longer recognizes, together with everything inside them. Backpack items are safe.

[size=5][b]Credits[/b][/size]

Applied Energistics 2, Refined Storage and Magic Storage for the genre. Built with [url=https://github.com/Garethp/Mods-of-Mistria-Installer]Mods of Mistria / MMAPI[/url], thanks to Garethp and its maintainers. And thanks to NPC Studio for shipping source readable enough to mod this deeply.

Source code: [url=https://github.com/Mihai-Tudosa/YADS]github.com/Mihai-Tudosa/YADS[/url]

Found a bug? Report it with your log file ([font=Courier New]%LOCALAPPDATA%\FieldsOfMistria\mod_data\yads\logs[/font]).

If YADS saved you an afternoon of chest-diving, you can buy me a coffee: [url=https://paypal.me/tudosamihai]paypal.me/tudosamihai[/url]. The mod is free and stays free.
